DESCRIPTION:Groundhog Day falls on February 2\, when a groundhog is lifted 
 from a stump on a hill outside Punxsutawney\, Pennsylvania and a man in a 
 top hat announces whether winter has six more weeks to run. The custom arr
 ived with German-speaking immigrants to Pennsylvania\, who had attached th
 e same Candlemas weather lore to a badger. It is also the rare American tr
 adition whose central claim a federal agency has tested and rejected: NOAA
 's published track record finds no predictive skill in it.\n\nhttps://toda
 ycelebrates.com/holiday/groundhog-day/
